<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#10120f">
<title>NIKO FOOTBALL LAB</title>
<style>
:root {
  --bg: #10120f;
  --panel: #1a1e19;
  --lime: #c6ff45;
  --muted: #a4ad9d;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: #f5f7f2;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  line-height: 1.5;
}
main { max-width: 850px; margin: auto; padding: 36px 20px 60px; }
.brand { color: var(--lime); font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: 3px; }
h1 { font-size: clamp(36px, 8vw, 64px); line-height: .98; margin: 20px 0; }
h1 span { color: var(--lime); }
p { color: var(--muted); }
.intro { max-width: 620px; font-size: 18px; }
.section { margin-top: 38px; }
.modules { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
article {
  background: var(--panel);
  border: 1px solid #30372d;
  border-radius: 14px;
  padding: 18px;
}
article h2 { font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 5px; }
article p { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; }
.tag { color: var(--lime); font-size: 11px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: 1.5px; }
.note {
  border-left: 3px solid var(--lime);
  padding: 12px 16px;
  background: var(--panel);
  border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0;
}
footer { margin-top: 45px; font-size: 12px; color: #778071; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <div class="brand">NIKO FOOTBALL LAB</div>
  <h1>ATTACKING PLAYER<br><span>DEVELOPMENT.</span></h1>
  <p class="intro">A 28-day technical development programme for wingers, forwards and attacking midfielders. Build sharper control, cleaner technique and more explosive actions.</p>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="tag">YOUR TRAINING PLAN</div>
    <h2>Technical modules</h2>
    <div class="modules">
      <article><div class="tag">MODULE 01</div><h2>Ball Mastery</h2><p>Close control, coordination and confidence on the ball.</p></article>
      <article><div class="tag">MODULE 02</div><h2>Passing & First Touch</h2><p>Improve wall passing, receiving and your first touch.</p></article>
      <article><div class="tag">MODULE 03</div><h2>Turns, Receiving & Acceleration</h2><p>Turn away from pressure and accelerate into space.</p></article>
      <article><div class="tag">MODULE 04</div><h2>Aerial Control</h2><p>Develop control and composure when receiving aerial balls.</p></article>
      <article><div class="tag">MODULE 05</div><h2>Aerial Passing</h2><p>Improve timing and accuracy with aerial passing.</p></article>
      <article><div class="tag">MODULE 06A</div><h2>Dynamic Dribbling</h2><p>Combine changes of direction, rhythm and speed.</p></article>
      <article><div class="tag">MODULE 06B</div><h2>Individual Creativity</h2><p>Practise creative actions and 1v1 solutions.</p></article>
      <article><div class="tag">MODULE 07A</div><h2>Explosive Power</h2><p>Build lower-body explosiveness for attacking actions.</p></article>
      <article><div class="tag">MODULE 07B</div><h2>Sprint Work</h2><p>Acceleration and sprint work: follow the programme instructions.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section note">
    <strong>TRAINING CONTENT</strong>
    <p>Video lessons and the downloadable programme will appear here when the media library is connected.</p>
  </section>
  <footer>© NIKO FOOTBALL LAB · ATTACKING PLAYER DEVELOPMENT</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
